# an open struct claims a label it accepted through ... for a struct or a list
# (#47's direction): the prior schema admits any value there, so declaring a
# type narrows it, even as an optional field. The converse of
# open-release-composite.
-- old.cue --
a!: string
...
-- new.cue --
a!: string
b?: {t!: string}
c?: [...string]
...
-- out --
incompatible
b is now {t!: string}, which does not accept every value of the prior _ (rule value-narrowed) @ new.cue:2:1
c is now [...string], which does not accept every value of the prior _ (rule value-narrowed) @ new.cue:3:1
